     "up": {"title":"Defining the field (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"Three CAPE students in Trinidad and Tobago answer a mock Paper 02 question: \"Describe the field of Information Technology. (3 marks)\". Which answer would earn the MOST marks?","options":[{"t":"IT is used in banking, tourism, health and education, and it has limitations such as GIGO and cost.","fb":"This gives some scope but never says what IT is or does, so it would earn only partial credit."},{"t":"IT is the use of computers to do work.","fb":"This is a one-line definition with no clear purpose and no example. It would earn one mark at most."},{"t":"IT is the use of computers, software, networks and telecommunications to capture, process, store, transmit and present information. As a field, it selects, manages and supports these technologies so organisations meet their information needs; for example, a bank's IT team keeps card terminals, servers and networks running so that transactions become account statements.","fb":"Correct. It names the technology, the purpose, what the field does and a specific example.","ok":true},{"t":"IT is the study of algorithms and how to make computers solve problems efficiently, for example designing faster ways to search records.","fb":"This is an accurate description of Computer Science, not IT, so it earns no marks here."}]}
