     "up": {"title":"Professional bodies at work (Challenge)","bloom":"Apply","intro":"<p>This time, name the body. Each activity below is a signature of ONE organisation.</p>","items":[{"text":"A researcher at Coralstone College searches a digital library of computing journals and conference papers run by the world's largest educational and scientific computing society. Which body runs it?","options":["ACM","AIS","IEEE","BCS"],"answer":0,"fb":"The ACM Digital Library is ACM's signature resource."},{"text":"An IT manager in Barbados is awarded Chartered IT Professional (CITP) status. Which body awards it?","options":["IEEE","ACM","BCS","AIS"],"answer":2,"fb":"CITP is awarded by BCS, The Chartered Institute for IT."},{"text":"Engineers revise the 802.11 standard so that new Wi-Fi routers sold in Guyana are faster but still work with older laptops. Which body develops this standard?","options":["AIS","ACM","BCS","IEEE"],"answer":3,"fb":"IEEE develops the 802 family of networking standards."},{"text":"An Information Systems lecturer from Jamaica presents her research at AMCIS. Which body runs this conference?","options":["IEEE","BCS","AIS","ACM"],"answer":2,"fb":"AMCIS, the Americas Conference on Information Systems, is run by AIS."},{"text":"A computer graphics researcher joins SIGGRAPH to share work on animation. SIGGRAPH is a Special Interest Group of which body?","options":["BCS","AIS","IEEE","ACM"],"answer":3,"fb":"SIGs, such as SIGGRAPH and SIGCHI, belong to ACM."},{"text":"A UK-based body examines a university's computing degree and confirms that it meets professional standards. Which body is this?","options":["ACM","BCS","AIS","IEEE"],"answer":1,"fb":"BCS accredits computing degrees."},{"text":"Working with ACM, which body develops the model curricula used by Information Systems departments?","options":["IEEE","IEEE Computer Society","BCS","AIS"],"answer":3,"fb":"AIS develops the IS model curricula jointly with ACM."}],"win":"Well done. Standards (IEEE), chartership and accreditation (BCS), digital library, SIGs and computing science (ACM), Information Systems research (AIS)."}
