     "up": {"title":"Answering a \"describe\" question (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"Ravi, a CAPE student in Chaguanas, is practising this Paper 02-style question: \"Discuss TWO limitations of IT for a small hotel in Nevis. (4 marks)\". His study group writes four answers. Which answer would earn ALL FOUR marks?","options":[{"t":"IT is expensive and it depends on electricity. These are two limitations that affect every hotel.","fb":"Two limitations are named, but neither is explained or linked to the hotel. This would earn about 2 marks."},{"t":"One limitation is GIGO: garbage in, garbage out. Another limitation is that staff may type booking dates wrongly.","fb":"Both points are really the same limitation (wrong input), so only one limitation is credited."},{"t":"First, IT depends on power and connectivity: if the island's network fails, the hotel's cloud booking system cannot take reservations, so it may lose guests unless it keeps a paper backup. Second, cost is a limitation: licences, support contracts and imported hardware are expensive for a small hotel, which may delay upgrades and leave it using outdated systems.","fb":"Correct. Two distinct limitations, each explained with a consequence for this hotel.","ok":true},{"t":"The hotel uses IT for bookings, card payments and guest Wi-Fi, which improves service and saves time.","fb":"This describes usage, not limitations, so it earns nothing for this question."}]}
