      "model": "<p><b>(a)</b> Information Technology is the use of computers, software and networks to capture, process, store, transmit and present information for people and organisations.</p><p><b>(b)</b> The hotel uses IT for online booking. This helps because guests can reserve a room from abroad at any time, even when the front desk is closed.</p><p><b>(c)</b> The power cut shows that IT depends on a reliable electricity supply; without power the system stops.</p><p><b>(d)</b> Another limitation of IT is garbage in, garbage out. For example, if a receptionist types the wrong dates, the guest gets the wrong bill.</p><p><b>(e)</b> The Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE) is a professional organisation that develops technical standards such as 802.11, which lets any brand of phone connect to the hotel's Wi-Fi.</p>",
