      "model": "<p><b>(a)</b> Computing is the umbrella term for all computer-related work, whereas Computer Science is one discipline that focuses on the theory of computation and algorithms.</p><p><b>(b)</b> The computer engineer would design the hardware and firmware for the payment kiosks. The software engineer would build and test the mobile app and keep it maintained. The IT specialist would set up the servers and network for the app and support staff and residents who have problems.</p><p><b>(c)</b> All five disciplines involve logical problem-solving.</p><p><b>(d)</b> Information Technology focuses on the technology infrastructure, such as servers and networks, and its users, whereas Information Systems focuses on how information and technology support the organisation's processes and management decisions.</p><p><b>(e)</b> The Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE) could help the IT specialist because it develops networking standards such as 802.11 and publishes journals that keep members up to date.</p>",
