     "up": {"title":"Which category of computer? (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>These systems are harder to place: a powerful machine is not always a supercomputer, and a small one is not always mobile. Sort each into the BEST category.</p>","bins":["Supercomputer","Mainframe","Minicomputer","Microcomputer","Mobile or embedded"],"items":[{"t":"An airline's reservation system must record every seat sale worldwide with almost no downtime.","bin":1,"fb":"Huge numbers of reliable transactions: a mainframe."},{"t":"A forecasting system runs global weather models to predict a hurricane's track towards Barbados.","bin":0,"fb":"Huge numerical models need maximum calculating speed: a supercomputer."},{"t":"The control unit inside a fuel pump at a petrol station in Grenada.","bin":4,"fb":"A computer built into a product to do one job: embedded."},{"t":"A laptop used by a nurse in Belize City to update patient notes.","bin":3,"fb":"A single-user, microprocessor-based machine: a microcomputer."},{"t":"A national statistics office needs 400 census clerks to enter records at once, all day, with no data loss.","bin":1,"fb":"Many simultaneous users, high volume and reliability: a mainframe."},{"t":"A climate centre runs a 100-year sea-level simulation for the Caribbean on thousands of processors working together.","bin":0,"fb":"One enormous calculation using massive parallel processing: a supercomputer."},{"t":"A high-end desktop workstation that one film editor in Port of Spain uses to edit 4K video.","bin":3,"fb":"Powerful, but still built around a microprocessor for one user: a microcomputer."},{"t":"A smartwatch that tracks a runner's heart rate in Kingston.","bin":4,"fb":"Small, wearable and battery-powered: mobile."},{"t":"A 1970s DEC VAX shared by the engineering department of a university in Trinidad and Tobago.","bin":2,"fb":"A departmental machine from that era: a minicomputer."}],"win":"Excellent judgement. Power alone does not decide the category: ask what the workload is and how many users share the machine."}
