     "up": {"title":"Software eras in Caribbean businesses (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>The consultant now asks clients to think like decision-makers. For each situation, choose the software approach or processing style that BEST fits the period and the need.</p>","items":[{"text":"In 1978, a large sugar company in Guyana needs a payroll system for its leased mainframe. No ready-made package exists for its machine. Which approach would it MOST likely use?","options":["Open-source mobile app","Cloud app","Custom-written program","Packaged spreadsheet"],"answer":2,"fb":"With no packages available, organisations paid programmers to write their own: custom software."},{"text":"In 1990, a small hardware store in Castries wants to track stock on its single PC without hiring a programmer.","options":["Cloud software","Custom-written program","Packaged software","Time-sharing on a mainframe"],"answer":2,"fb":"Ready-made packages let small businesses computerise cheaply on one microcomputer."},{"text":"Today, a tour operator in St. Kitts wants bookings available on staff phones anywhere, with nothing to install and a monthly fee.","options":["Packaged software on one PC","Cloud software (software as a service)","An MS-DOS application","Custom mainframe program"],"answer":1,"fb":"Software delivered through a browser for a subscription is cloud software."},{"text":"A school in Belize wants a full operating system and a browser with no licence cost, and the right to modify the code.","options":["Open-source software","Custom-written program","Packaged commercial software","Batch processing system"],"answer":0,"fb":"Freely available, modifiable source code is open-source software."},{"text":"In the 1960s, a university computer runs student jobs one after another, automatically, from a queue of punched cards, with no user interaction.","options":["Touch interface","Time-sharing","Batch processing","Graphical user interface"],"answer":2,"fb":"Jobs run in sequence with no interaction: batch processing."},{"text":"Around 1970, staff at many terminals use one computer at the same time, each seeming to have it to themselves.","options":["Time-sharing","Batch processing","Packaged software","Touch interface"],"answer":0,"fb":"Sharing the processor among many interactive users is time-sharing."},{"text":"A bank in Barbados still runs a decades-old COBOL system because rewriting it would be costly and risky. What does this show?","options":["COBOL is a mobile operating system","Open-source software cannot run in banks","Packaged software replaced every custom program by 1990","Software eras overlap: older custom systems stay in use alongside new apps"],"answer":3,"fb":"Eras overlap. Legacy systems often outlive the period in which they were written."}],"win":"Well analysed. The right approach depended on what was available at the time and on the size and needs of the organisation."}
