     "up": {"title":"Language, operating system or application? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Classify each milestone. Watch for traps: a language famous for building an operating system is still a language, and a system written in a language is still application software.</p>","items":[{"text":"C (1972), used to rewrite UNIX","options":["Programming language","Operating system","Application software"],"answer":0,"fb":"C is a language, even though it is famous for writing operating systems."},{"text":"OS/360, which managed jobs and devices on IBM System/360 mainframes","options":["Operating system","Programming language","Application software"],"answer":0,"fb":"It managed the machine's resources: an operating system."},{"text":"Lotus 1-2-3 (1983), the spreadsheet that made the IBM PC a business tool","options":["Operating system","Application software","Programming language"],"answer":1,"fb":"A spreadsheet does a job for the user: application software."},{"text":"Linux (1991), released free with its source code","options":["Operating system","Programming language","Application software"],"answer":0,"fb":"Being open source does not change its job: Linux is an operating system."},{"text":"Firefox, an open-source web browser","options":["Programming language","Application software","Operating system"],"answer":1,"fb":"A browser is an application that runs on an operating system."},{"text":"iOS (2007), which runs the iPhone's touch interface","options":["Operating system","Programming language","Application software"],"answer":0,"fb":"iOS is a mobile operating system."},{"text":"Java (1995), designed so that programs can run on many kinds of computer","options":["Application software","Programming language","Operating system"],"answer":1,"fb":"Java is a programming language."},{"text":"A bank's payroll system, written in COBOL","options":["Application software","Operating system","Programming language"],"answer":0,"fb":"The payroll system is application software. COBOL is only the language it was written in."},{"text":"WordStar (1978), an early word processor","options":["Application software","Operating system","Programming language"],"answer":0,"fb":"A word processor is application software for end users."}],"win":"Sharp work. Classify by the job the software does, not by what it is associated with."}
