     "up": {"title":"Build the Internet timeline (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>The open-day poster now has ten milestones and no dates. Put them in order, earliest first.</p>","blocks":[{"t":"Packet switching is proposed as a way to send data across a network."},{"t":"ARPANET links four university and research sites."},{"t":"Ray Tomlinson sends network email using the @ sign."},{"t":"Cerf and Kahn describe the TCP/IP protocols."},{"t":"ARPANET switches over to TCP/IP, and the Internet is born."},{"t":"The first .com names are registered under the Domain Name System."},{"t":"Tim Berners-Lee creates the World Wide Web at CERN."},{"t":"The Mosaic graphical browser brings the Web to the public."},{"t":"Broadband, search engines and social media spread."},{"t":"Smartphones make the mobile Internet mainstream."}],"win":"Correct. TCP/IP was described in 1974 but adopted in 1983, and the Web came only after the Internet and DNS were in place."}
