     "up": {"title":"From telegraph to 5G (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>The media club's feature now has ten milestones and no dates. Watch the close pair in the middle: did analogue mobile phones or the first transatlantic fibre cable come first? Put them in order, earliest first.</p>","blocks":[{"t":"Morse sends coded pulses along wires with the electric telegraph."},{"t":"Bell patents the telephone, carrying voice over copper wires."},{"t":"Marconi sends a radio signal across the Atlantic."},{"t":"Telstar relays live television across the Atlantic by satellite."},{"t":"1G analogue mobile phone networks begin, first in Japan."},{"t":"TAT-8, the first transatlantic fibre-optic cable, carries data as pulses of light."},{"t":"2G GSM brings digital mobile calls and SMS text messages."},{"t":"3G networks make mobile data practical."},{"t":"4G LTE brings mobile broadband and video to smartphones."},{"t":"5G offers very high speed and low latency."}],"win":"Excellent. 1G (1979) came before TAT-8 (1988), and each mobile generation shifted further from voice towards data."}
