     "stimulus": "<p class=\"passage\">When Hurricane Irma struck the Turks and Caicos Islands in September 2017, many residents lost phone and Internet service. Families overseas waited for news, businesses could not process card payments, and engineers worked to restore towers and cables. The island's links to the world now depend on fibre-optic submarine cables, mobile networks and the Internet, technologies with a long history.</p>",
     "prompt": "<p>Refer to the passage and your own knowledge.</p><ol type=\"a\"><li>Outline FOUR key stages in the history of the Internet, from its origins to the World Wide Web. <i>(6 marks)</i></li><li>Outline the development of telecommunications from the telegraph to modern mobile networks, naming THREE stages. <i>(5 marks)</i></li><li>Explain TWO reasons why resilient telecommunications infrastructure is especially important for a small island such as the Turks and Caicos Islands. <i>(4 marks)</i></li></ol>",
     "min": 220,
