     "up": {"title":"Traditional or electronic? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>The librarian at a school in Montego Bay, Jamaica is relabelling the collection. Several items have the same <b>content</b> in a different <b>medium</b>. Sort each one by what the reader needs in order to use it.</p>","main":"Is this a traditional or an electronic source?","bins":["Traditional","Electronic"],"items":[{"t":"A printed product catalogue posted by a supplier","bin":0,"fb":"Print that needs no device: traditional."},{"t":"A forwarded WhatsApp voice note from an eyewitness","bin":1,"fb":"Social media messaging needs a device: electronic."},{"t":"The e-paper edition of a daily newspaper read on a tablet","bin":1,"fb":"A newspaper, but delivered in a digital medium: electronic."},{"t":"The old card catalogue in wooden drawers","bin":0,"fb":"Printed cards need no device: traditional."},{"t":"The library's online public access catalogue (OPAC)","bin":1,"fb":"Same purpose as the card catalogue, but it is searched on a computer: electronic."},{"t":"The e-book version of the Form 5 IT textbook","bin":1,"fb":"Same content as the printed book, but it needs a device: electronic."},{"t":"A retired teacher interviewed face to face about the 1988 hurricane","bin":0,"fb":"People are a traditional source."},{"t":"A podcast episode interviewing a fisherman from Port Royal","bin":1,"fb":"Audio that needs a device to play: electronic."},{"t":"A printed copy of a wiki page pinned to the notice board","bin":0,"fb":"The content came from a wiki, but the copy on the board is paper: traditional."},{"t":"A printed transcript of a radio interview, kept in a folder","bin":0,"fb":"The interview was broadcast, but this copy is on paper: traditional."}],"win":"Well sorted. Classification follows the medium in front of the reader, not where the content came from: a printed wiki page is traditional, and an e-book is electronic."}
