     "up": {"title":"Using the library: advantage or disadvantage? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Keisha, an Upper Six student in Kingstown, St. Vincent, uses the public library for a project on e-commerce. Some of her experiences show the library overcoming a weakness of print; others show real limits. Sort each one.</p>","main":"Is this an advantage or a disadvantage of a library as an information source?","bins":["Advantage of a library","Disadvantage of a library"],"items":[{"t":"The library holds the only surviving copies of a 1979 local newspaper.","bin":0,"fb":"Libraries preserve local material that is not online: an advantage."},{"t":"The study room gives her a quiet place with reliable Wi-Fi.","bin":0,"fb":"Study space, computers and Internet access: an advantage."},{"t":"Books are classified by subject, so she finds three related titles beside the one she wanted.","bin":0,"fb":"Organised collections make sources easier to find: an advantage."},{"t":"Her library login lets her read journal articles from home after the building has closed.","bin":0,"fb":"Libraries give access to paid electronic sources, which also softens the opening-hours problem: an advantage."},{"t":"The newest book on e-commerce in the collection was published in 2012.","bin":1,"fb":"Limited budgets can leave stock out of date: a disadvantage."},{"t":"She may borrow only three books, and two that she needs have waiting lists.","bin":1,"fb":"Borrowing limits and limited copies: a disadvantage."},{"t":"The last bus from her village leaves town at 4 p.m.","bin":1,"fb":"Users must travel to the building: a disadvantage."},{"t":"Her overdue fine is more than her bus fare.","bin":1,"fb":"Fines are a cost of using the library: a disadvantage."},{"t":"A librarian shows her how to use subject headings to cut 300 results to 12.","bin":0,"fb":"Trained staff help users search and choose sources: an advantage."},{"t":"After a storm, the reading room closes for a month for repairs.","bin":1,"fb":"Physical buildings and collections are vulnerable to storms: a disadvantage."}],"win":"Well done. Libraries give free, expert-supported access to organised and archived sources, including electronic ones; their limits are stock, copies, travel, fines and vulnerability to storms."}
