     "up": {"title":"Choose the most suitable source (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>Each need has a constraint: speed, expertise, offline use, exact wording or local opinion. Choose the source whose strengths fit BOTH the need and the constraint.</p>","items":[{"text":"A journalist in Kingston must confirm, within the hour, whether a bridge in St. Ann has collapsed, after a video goes viral.","options":["A phone call to the police or the works agency","The comments under the video","Tomorrow's newspaper","A geography textbook"],"answer":0,"fb":"A person with first-hand, official knowledge can confirm or deny it quickly. Comments are unchecked; the newspaper is too late."},{"text":"A university researcher needs peer-reviewed studies from the last five years on sargassum in the eastern Caribbean.","options":["An electronic database of journals, filtered by date","A news web site","A travel blog","A library catalogue"],"answer":0,"fb":"The database holds selected journal research and its filters limit results to the last five years. A catalogue only lists items the library holds."},{"text":"A teacher in the Guyana interior with no Internet needs an animated explanation of the water cycle.","options":["A web site","A wiki","A DVD","An electronic database"],"answer":2,"fb":"A DVD carries animation and works offline. The other three need a connection."},{"text":"A student in Barbados needs the exact words of the Prime Minister's budget speech.","options":["The official transcript or recording of the speech","A magazine feature","A blog summary","A newspaper editorial about the speech"],"answer":0,"fb":"Only the primary source gives the exact words, with no one else's interpretation."},{"text":"A shop owner in Providenciales wants to know which laptops her own customers want this season.","options":["A short questionnaire for her customers","A supplier catalogue","A retail textbook","A computing magazine review"],"answer":0,"fb":"Only her customers know their own preferences. The catalogue shows what is available, not what they want."},{"text":"A Form 4 student in Antigua needs a structured beginner's explanation of how computers developed, with diagrams.","options":["A journal article","A textbook","A social media thread","A daily newspaper"],"answer":1,"fb":"A textbook gives depth, logical structure and diagrams at a beginner's level; a journal is too technical."},{"text":"A tour operator in Castries needs today's cruise-ship arrival times.","options":["Last month's tourism magazine","A book on Caribbean tourism","The port authority's official web site","A wiki"],"answer":2,"fb":"Live, official and updated daily: the official web site. The magazine and book are out of date for this purpose."}],"win":"Excellent judgement. The best source is the one whose advantages match the need and whose disadvantages do not matter in that situation."}
