     "up": {"title":"Traditional or electronic: which has the edge? (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>Some of these situations follow the general pattern, and some test its exceptions. Decide which group of sources has the edge in each one.</p>","main":"In this situation, which group of sources has the edge?","bins":["Traditional sources have the edge","Electronic sources have the edge"],"items":[{"t":"A student on Saba needs to search 5,000 articles for \"desalination\" in seconds.","bin":1,"fb":"Keyword searching is a key electronic strength."},{"t":"A teacher wants students to hear a calypsonian explain how his lyrics changed over time.","bin":1,"fb":"Audio is multimedia, which electronic sources carry."},{"t":"Thirty students across Jamaica need the same reading at the same time.","bin":1,"fb":"Electronic sources allow many simultaneous users."},{"t":"A town council needs a source that still works when the island's undersea Internet cable is cut.","bin":0,"fb":"Traditional sources do not depend on network infrastructure."},{"t":"A family in rural Belize with no data plan needs instructions for purifying water.","bin":0,"fb":"Print and people need no device or data plan."},{"t":"A student must read and annotate a long text for hours, with no charger available.","bin":0,"fb":"Print needs no battery and is easy to annotate."},{"t":"An archive must still be readable in 50 years without depending on a file format or device.","bin":0,"fb":"Paper does not become obsolete with a file format, although it must be protected from water and fire."},{"t":"During a week-long power cut in Dominica, a student must revise for CAPE.","bin":0,"fb":"Traditional sources need no power or connection."},{"t":"A researcher on Barbuda needs peer-reviewed articles at 2 a.m.","bin":1,"fb":"An exception to \"electronic means unchecked\": an electronic journal database is checked AND available at any hour."},{"t":"A reporter needs passenger figures updated this morning.","bin":1,"fb":"Online sources can be updated instantly."}],"win":"Well judged. You applied the general pattern and spotted its exceptions, such as electronic databases that are both checked and available all night."}
