     "up": {"title":"Which characteristic is being described? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Students at Flamboyant Heights College are describing sources, and several comments contain two clues. Choose the characteristic each comment is MAINLY about.</p>","items":[{"text":"\"It's free on the ministry site, but the site is down every afternoon during power rationing.\"","options":["Cost","Reliability","Currency","Availability"],"answer":3,"fb":"\"Free\" mentions cost, but the point of the comment is that the student often cannot get the source: availability."},{"text":"\"The 2025 report uses population figures from the 2011 census.\"","options":["Breadth of coverage","Depth","Currency","Reliability"],"answer":2,"fb":"The cover date is recent, but the data is old. Currency covers when the information was produced."},{"text":"\"It lists all 15 CARICOM members' electricity tariffs, but in a single table row each.\"","options":["Depth","Cost","Format","Breadth of coverage"],"answer":3,"fb":"The comment stresses how widely it covers the region: breadth. One row each also shows it is shallow."},{"text":"\"It's a captioned video on the council's channel on a video-sharing site.\"","options":["Availability","Format and medium","Reliability","Cost"],"answer":1,"fb":"Captioned video is the format; the video-sharing site is the medium."},{"text":"\"Three editions of this almanac give the same rainfall totals as the meteorological service.\"","options":["Breadth of coverage","Reliability","Availability","Currency"],"answer":1,"fb":"Consistency with itself and with an official source: reliability."},{"text":"\"Transcribing the two-hour interview cost me a whole weekend.\"","options":["Depth","Currency","Availability","Cost"],"answer":3,"fb":"Time is a cost, even when no money is spent."},{"text":"\"The engineer I need to interview is overseas until after my deadline.\"","options":["Cost","Depth","Reliability","Availability"],"answer":3,"fb":"People as sources have availability too."}],"win":"Sharp reading. When a comment has two clues, ask what the speaker is mainly worried about."}
