     "up": {"title":"Manual or automated? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","q":"At Frangipani Hill Academy, the form teacher marks a paper register each morning. A clerk types the absences into a spreadsheet, which counts each student's absences for the term, and the office system automatically emails parents when a student passes five absences. Which analysis is MOST accurate?","options":[{"t":"It is fully automated, because the counting and the emails are done by computer.","fb":"Two automated stages do not make the whole system automated; the register is still marked by hand."},{"t":"It is fully manual, because the data begins on paper.","fb":"The starting point is manual, but processing and output are automated."},{"t":"Collection and entry are done by people, while the counting and the emails are automated, so it is a mixed system.","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. The analysis works stage by stage: people collect and key the data; software processes it and produces the output."},{"t":"Input is automated because the clerk types the data into a computer.","fb":"A person reading a register and keying it in is still people doing the input; no device captures the data directly."}]}
