     "up": {"title":"Manual or automated input? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Some of these activities are not input at all. Decide whether each is <b>manual input</b>, <b>automated input</b> (a device reads the data directly from its source), or a <b>different stage</b> of the cycle.</p>","main":"Manual input, automated input, or another stage?","bins":["Manual input","Automated input","Not input: another stage"],"items":[{"t":"A census officer ticks answers on a paper questionnaire.","bin":0,"fb":"Data collected by hand on a source document: manual input."},{"t":"A nurse in Georgetown writes a patient's blood pressure on a paper chart.","bin":0,"fb":"A person reads and records the value: manual input."},{"t":"A chip card reader at a till reads the customer's card.","bin":1,"fb":"The device reads the data directly: automated input."},{"t":"The records are backed up to cloud storage overnight.","bin":2,"fb":"Backing up is part of the storage stage."},{"t":"A market vendor ticks a tally sheet each time she sells a coconut.","bin":0,"fb":"Tally marks by hand: manual input."},{"t":"The database sorts patient records by surname.","bin":2,"fb":"Sorting is a processing operation."},{"t":"A cashier scans each item's barcode.","bin":1,"fb":"The scanner reads the code; the cashier only holds the item: automated input."},{"t":"A tide gauge sensor logs the sea level every minute.","bin":1,"fb":"A sensor captures data without a person: automated input."},{"t":"An OMR machine reads the shaded bubbles on answer sheets.","bin":1,"fb":"Optical mark recognition: automated input."},{"t":"The till prints a receipt for the customer.","bin":2,"fb":"A receipt is output, not input."}],"win":"Well sorted. Input gets data into the system: manually when a person records it, automatically when a device reads it at source. Printing, sorting and backing up belong to other stages."}
