     "up": {"title":"Match the processing operation (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>A health ministry in the region tracks dengue cases. Match each operation to its example. Three operations belong to other stages of the cycle, so label those carefully.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"Collating","r":"Merging the overnight uploads from twelve health centres into one table"},{"l":"Calculating","r":"Working out the number of cases per 1,000 residents in each district"},{"l":"Sorting","r":"Arranging districts in descending order of cases per 1,000 residents"},{"l":"Analysing","r":"Finding that cases rise about four weeks after heavy rain"},{"l":"Presenting (output)","r":"Turning the results into a colour-coded map of the districts"},{"l":"Dissemination (output)","r":"Sending the map to every health centre by email and SMS link"},{"l":"Retrieving (storage)","r":"Calling up last year's figures from the database to compare them"}],"win":"Correct. Collating, calculating, sorting and analysing are processing; presenting and dissemination are output; retrieving belongs to storage. Naming the stage as well as the operation earns the marks."}
