     "up": {"title":"Which processing operation? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","q":"At Willemstad Taxi Association, a clerk (1) puts all 30 drivers' weekly trip sheets into one folder; (2) adds up the fares on each driver's sheets; (3) arranges the drivers from highest to lowest weekly earnings; and (4) notices that drivers who work the cruise pier earn twice as much on ship days. Which list correctly names operations 1 to 4?","options":[{"t":"Collating, analysing, sorting, presenting","fb":"Step 2 is arithmetic (calculating), and step 4 finds a pattern (analysing). Presenting would be producing a chart or report."},{"t":"Collecting, calculating, sorting, disseminating","fb":"Collecting is input, and disseminating is distributing output. Steps 1 and 4 are collating and analysing."},{"t":"Collating, calculating, sorting, analysing","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. Bringing sheets together is collating, adding is calculating, ordering by earnings is sorting, and finding a pattern is analysing."},{"t":"Sorting, calculating, collating, analysing","fb":"Step 1 gathers sheets into one set (collating); step 3 orders them by a key (sorting). These two are reversed."}]}
