     "up": {"title":"Storing, retrieving or transmitting? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>A medical centre in Castries handles patient records. Some activities involve a network, but the network does not decide the answer: ask whether the record is being <b>kept</b>, <b>brought back for use</b> or <b>sent somewhere else</b>.</p>","main":"Which activity is this MAINLY?","bins":["Storing","Retrieving","Transmitting"],"items":[{"t":"A clerk files a new patient card in the drawer for surnames beginning with R.","bin":0,"fb":"Placing a record in its home: storing."},{"t":"A nightly job copies the whole database to a second server in another territory.","bin":0,"fb":"The copy travels over a network, but its purpose is a stored copy kept for recovery: storing."},{"t":"A courier carries a sealed envelope of test results to the hospital.","bin":2,"fb":"Physically moving records: manual transmitting."},{"t":"A doctor opens last year's blood results to compare them with today's.","bin":1,"fb":"Bringing back stored results: retrieving."},{"t":"Old X-ray images are archived on a separate drive and labelled by year.","bin":0,"fb":"Keeping records for future use: storing."},{"t":"Results flow automatically from the laboratory's system into the centre's records.","bin":2,"fb":"Moving data between systems: automated transmitting."},{"t":"A nurse searches the database for every diabetic patient over 60.","bin":1,"fb":"A query that finds and brings back records: retrieving."},{"t":"A receptionist pulls a patient's folder from the cabinet before an appointment.","bin":1,"fb":"Taking a stored record out for use: manual retrieving."},{"t":"Each consultation note is saved to the server the moment the doctor clicks Save.","bin":0,"fb":"Saving to a server: automated storing."},{"t":"An X-ray is sent securely to a specialist in Curaçao.","bin":2,"fb":"Sending to another location: transmitting."}],"win":"Well done. A network can be used for all three; the purpose decides the activity. Storing keeps records, retrieving brings them back, and transmitting sends them elsewhere."}
