     "up": {"title":"Open all hours (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"Kralendijk Crafts Co-op on Kaya Grandi closes at 6 p.m. Since it opened an online shop, 40% of its orders arrive between midnight and 6 a.m., mostly from buyers in Europe who read the shop in Dutch or French and pay in euros. Which statement BEST evaluates the advantages shown?","options":[{"t":"New types of jobs is the main advantage, because a website needs a designer.","fb":"No new job is described in the stem. Evaluate the evidence given, not what might have happened."},{"t":"Cost effectiveness is the main advantage, because the co-op no longer needs staff.","fb":"The stem does not say staff were cut; the crafts still have to be made and shipped."},{"t":"Only communication is shown, because the shop sends order confirmations.","fb":"Confirmations are not mentioned, and communication is not the point of the stem: trading around the clock and across languages is."},{"t":"Availability is the main advantage, because orders arrive while the shop is closed; the multilingual European sales also show globalisation reducing language and distance barriers.","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. It identifies the main advantage and recognises a second one supported by the evidence."}]}
