     "up": {"title":"File a new record by hand (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>A new student joins a school in Castries that keeps its records in a manual alphabetical file. Put all seven steps in order, including the checks that stop errors and duplicates.</p>","blocks":[{"t":"Copy her details from the enrolment form onto a blank record card."},{"t":"Check the card against the enrolment form for missing fields and the spelling of her surname."},{"t":"Identify the filing key: her surname."},{"t":"Open the drawer at the divider for the first letter of her surname."},{"t":"Check that no card already exists for her, to avoid a duplicate record."},{"t":"Insert the card in its alphabetical position, using her first name if another student has the same surname."},{"t":"Finally, update the record count on the box index and file the enrolment form as the source document."}],"win":"Correct. Manual filing is the cycle in miniature: input from a source document, checks for accuracy and duplicates, a filing key, storage in order, and an update to the index."}
