     "up": {"title":"Match the representation to the job (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>A tourism and education office in Barbados has eight jobs to publish. Several representations could work for some of them; match each to the one that does the job BEST.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"Table","r":"Exact high- and low-tide times for every day next week"},{"l":"Line graph","r":"How a patient's temperature changed every hour overnight"},{"l":"Bar chart","r":"Comparing cruise calls at five Caribbean ports in March"},{"l":"Pie chart","r":"What share of a household's monthly budget goes to rent, food, transport and savings"},{"l":"Scatter graph","r":"Whether students who study more hours tend to score higher"},{"l":"Pictogram","r":"Showing Grade 2 pupils how many mangoes each class collected, one picture per ten mangoes"},{"l":"Graphic (icon or map)","r":"Showing visitors who speak different languages where the taxis and toilets are"},{"l":"Text","r":"Explaining the conditions under which a scholarship can be withdrawn"}],"win":"Very good. Exact look-up, trend, comparison, share of a whole, relationship, young audience, recognition across languages and explanation each have a best-fit representation."}
