     "up": {"title":"Notations quick-fire (Challenge)","bloom":"Apply","intro":"<p>Students in a cross-subject project in Port of Spain must now apply notations, not just name them. Answer each question.</p>","items":[{"text":"In 4/4 time, which combination fills exactly one bar?","options":["Three crotchets","A semibreve and a quaver","Two minims and a crotchet","A minim and two crotchets"],"answer":3,"fb":"2 + 1 + 1 = 4 beats. The others make 5, 4½ and 3 beats."},{"text":"A note was sharpened earlier in the bar. A natural sign ♮ before the same note tells the player to...","options":["rest for one beat","play it loudly","cancel the sharp and play the note at its natural pitch","play it a semitone higher again"],"answer":2,"fb":"The natural cancels a sharp or flat."},{"text":"How many atoms does one molecule of CO₂ contain in total?","options":["3","4","2"],"answer":0,"fb":"One carbon atom and two oxygen atoms: three in total."},{"text":"The distance from Earth to the Sun is about 1.5 × 10⁸ km. Written in full, this is...","options":["150,000,000 km","15,000,000 km","1,500,000,000 km"],"answer":0,"fb":"1.5 × 100,000,000 = 150,000,000."},{"text":"The spreadsheet formula =AVERAGE(B2:B6) is an example of...","options":["mathematical notation adapted for computing","musical notation","Morse Code"],"answer":0,"fb":"Spreadsheet formulas are a computing form of mathematical notation."},{"text":"Which is the main DISADVANTAGE of special-purpose notations?","options":["They are meaningless to people who have not learned the rules","They mean different things in different countries","They are long and wordy"],"answer":0,"fb":"They are concise and universal for trained readers, but untrained readers cannot interpret them."},{"text":"On an electricity bill, \"412 kWh\" means...","options":["412 kilometres per hour","412 kilowatt-hours of energy used","412 kilograms of water heated"],"answer":1,"fb":"kWh is the SI-based symbol for kilowatt-hours, a unit of energy."}],"win":"Excellent. You applied musical, scientific and mathematical notations accurately, which is exactly what \"identify, with an example\" questions reward."}
