     "up": {"title":"Morse at Fort George (Challenge)","bloom":"Apply","intro":"<p>Fort George Signal Club's advanced trainees must encode, decode and work out timings. Use the Morse table and the timing rules: dot 1 unit, dash 3 units, gap inside a letter 1 unit, between letters 3, between words 7.</p>","items":[{"text":"Decode: <b>-.-. --- .- ... -</b>","options":["KOAST","COATS","COAST"],"answer":2,"fb":"-.-. = C, --- = O, .- = A, ... = S, - = T."},{"text":"Which is the correct Morse for STORM?","options":["... -- --- .-. -","... - --- .-.. --","... - --- .-. --"],"answer":2,"fb":"S ..., T -, O ---, R .-., M --. The second option has L (.-..) and the third spells SMORT."},{"text":"How many time units does the letter S (...) take, from the start of the first dot to the end of the last?","options":["5 units","7 units","3 units"],"answer":0,"fb":"Three dots (3 units) plus two 1-unit gaps inside the letter: 5 units."},{"text":"How many time units does the letter O (---) take?","options":["11 units","9 units","13 units"],"answer":0,"fb":"Three dashes (9 units) plus two 1-unit gaps: 11 units."},{"text":"A receiver hears a dot, a 1-unit gap and a dash; then a 3-unit gap; then a dash, a 1-unit gap and a dot. What was sent?","options":["NA","AN","R"],"answer":1,"fb":"The 3-unit gap separates two letters: .- (A) then -. (N)."},{"text":"Why is Morse valued for emergencies in poor conditions?","options":["It uses 8 bits per letter","The receiver only needs to tell short from long signals and gaps, so a weak, noisy signal can still be read","Every letter has the same length"],"answer":1,"fb":"Two easily distinguished elements make Morse robust in noise."},{"text":"Which statement comparing Morse with ASCII binary is MOST accurate?","options":["They are the same code sent in different ways","Morse is a form of binary place value","Both use two basic elements, but Morse also relies on gap lengths and uses variable-length codes, while ASCII uses fixed-length patterns"],"answer":2,"fb":"Timing gaps and variable lengths are what make Morse different from fixed-length binary codes."}],"win":"Excellent signalling. You can encode, decode, calculate timings and explain how Morse differs from binary codes."}
