     "up": {"title":"Read the byte (Challenge)","bloom":"Apply","intro":"<p>Palm Beach Marina's computer stores its counts in single bytes. These patterns are harder: write 128 64 32 16 8 4 2 1 above each one and add the place values where there is a 1.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"10101010","r":"Life jackets in store: 170"},{"l":"01111111","r":"Berths occupied: 127"},{"l":"11001000","r":"Visitors on the dock today: 200"},{"l":"00110111","r":"Seats sold on the ferry: 55"},{"l":"10000000","r":"Boats in the lagoon: 128"},{"l":"7 bits","r":"128 possible patterns, enough for standard ASCII"},{"l":"16 bits (two bytes)","r":"65,536 possible patterns"}],"win":"Well read. You added place values (not 1s), and you know that n bits give 2ⁿ patterns."}
