     "up": {"title":"Convert 26 to binary by division (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Convert 26 to binary by repeated division, then check it and extend it. Each step also says which place value its remainder becomes, so notice why the remainders must be read from the bottom up.</p>","blocks":[{"t":"26 ÷ 2 = 13 remainder 0 (this remainder is the 1s bit)"},{"t":"13 ÷ 2 = 6 remainder 1 (the 2s bit)"},{"t":"6 ÷ 2 = 3 remainder 0 (the 4s bit)"},{"t":"3 ÷ 2 = 1 remainder 1 (the 8s bit)"},{"t":"1 ÷ 2 = 0 remainder 1 (the 16s bit); the quotient is 0, so stop"},{"t":"Read the remainders from the bottom up: 11010"},{"t":"Pad with leading zeros to 8 bits: 00011010"},{"t":"Check with place values: 16 + 8 + 2 = 26"},{"t":"Extend: shifting every bit one place left gives 00110100, which is 52, double 26"}],"win":"Exactly right. The first remainder is the least significant bit, which is why you read upwards. Checking with place values, and noticing that a left shift doubles the value, shows real understanding."}
