     "up": {"title":"Choose the most appropriate tool (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>Each scenario adds a constraint: security, weak bandwidth, a lasting archive, an easy way to leave, encryption. Choose the tool that meets the need AND the constraint.</p>","items":[{"text":"A school in Saba must send a 3 GB coursework folder, and the exam board requires a secure, logged transfer.","options":["A secure FTP (SFTP) upload","An email attachment","A social media post","A cross-platform messaging group"],"answer":0,"fb":"The file is far too big for email, and a secure FTP version protects it in transit with controlled accounts."},{"text":"A nurse on St. Eustatius must discuss an X-ray live with a specialist in Curaçao, but the clinic's connection is weak.","options":["A telnet session","SMS","A web conference with video switched off and the X-ray shared on screen","A mailing list"],"answer":2,"fb":"Real-time discussion with screen sharing; switching video off saves bandwidth on a weak connection."},{"text":"A farmers' group in Dominica wants answers about crop disease kept, organised by topic and searchable by future members.","options":["VoIP","A cross-platform messaging group","A discussion forum","A message board"],"answer":2,"fb":"Threads by topic and a searchable archive. A group chat buries answers; a message board is less structured."},{"text":"A charity in Trinidad sends a monthly newsletter to 3,000 donors and must let them leave easily.","options":["A discussion forum","A mailing list with an unsubscribe link","A web conference","A group chat"],"answer":1,"fb":"A mailing list pushes the newsletter to inboxes, and subscribers can unsubscribe."},{"text":"A family in Kingstown on Android phones shares photos daily with relatives in London on iPhones, and wants messages encrypted end to end.","options":["Telnet","A public social media page","A cross-platform messaging tool with end-to-end encryption","SMS"],"answer":2,"fb":"Works across operating systems, carries rich media and, in some apps, encrypts messages by default."},{"text":"An IT technician in Kingstown must run commands on a server in the Kingston office without exposing the password.","options":["Telnet, because it uses little bandwidth","VoIP","FTP","SSH, the encrypted replacement for telnet"],"answer":3,"fb":"Telnet would send the password as plain text; SSH encrypts the remote session."},{"text":"A student needs peer-reviewed articles on submarine cables AND today's official notice from the port authority.","options":["A mailing list","FTP","A search engine with advanced operators, plus the port authority's official online service","Telnet"],"answer":2,"fb":"Search skills find the research; the official online service gives the current notice directly from its source."}],"win":"Strong choices. Each tool fits the data, the timing and the audience, and also meets the extra constraint of security, bandwidth, archive or encryption."}
