     "up": {"title":"Spot the valid disadvantages (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>A Form 6 student in Grenada listed twelve \"disadvantages\" of the tools a business uses. Several are misconceptions that would lose marks. Check each one against the tool's definition.</p>","q":"Tap EVERY line that states an ACCURATE disadvantage.","lines":["1. Standard telnet sends usernames and passwords as plain text.","2. SMS cannot be received on a basic mobile phone.","3. VoIP call quality falls when bandwidth is low or latency is high.","4. A mailing list requires every member to visit a website to read messages.","5. Web conferencing requires participants to be available at the same time.","6. Search engine results can include biased, out-of-date or paid pages.","7. FTP can only download files and cannot upload them.","8. Cross-platform messaging works only if both users have the same brand of phone.","9. Discussion forums need moderation to remove spam and abuse.","10. Each SMS is limited to about 160 characters of standard text.","11. Emergency services may not automatically receive a VoIP caller's location.","12. A web conference always leaves a written record of everything said."],"correct":[0,2,4,5,8,9,10],"win":"Correct. Lines 2, 4, 7, 8 and 12 are misconceptions: SMS works on basic phones, mailing lists push to inboxes, FTP uploads and downloads, cross-platform tools work across different phones, and a web conference leaves no record unless it is recorded.","miss":"Check each line against the tool's definition. \"Cross-platform\" means across different devices and systems, and real-time tools leave no record unless someone records them."}
