     "up": {"title":"Build the justification chain (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>The Dawn Beach Kayak Tours must remind guests the evening before of the 8 a.m. start. Some guests are visitors with no local data plan. Put the five links of the chain in order, then add the rejected alternative and the conclusion that turn it into a Grade One answer.</p>","blocks":[{"t":"Need: every guest must receive tomorrow's 8 a.m. start time tonight, including visitors with no local data plan."},{"t":"Tool: send each guest an SMS reminder."},{"t":"Feature: SMS travels over the cellular network and works on any mobile phone without data or an app."},{"t":"Benefit: all guests, including visitors without data, receive the time, so fewer people miss the launch."},{"t":"Drawback weighed: each SMS has a small cost, but one short reminder per booking is far cheaper than a missed trip."},{"t":"Alternative rejected: a messaging-app reminder was rejected because guests without local data might not see it until morning."},{"t":"Conclusion: SMS is the most reliable tool for this reminder, with the booking receipt sent separately by email as a record."}],"win":"Correct. Need, Tool, Feature, Benefit, Drawback weighed, then an alternative rejected with a scenario-based reason and a clear conclusion. Every link mentions something specific to the kayak company."}
