     "up": {"title":"Forum or mailing list? (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"Willemstad Softball Association wants (1) fixtures and announcements to reach all 400 members reliably, and (2) a place where members' questions are answered once and stay available to everyone. Which recommendation is BEST justified?","options":[{"t":"A message board for both needs, because posts always stay at the top.","fb":"The opposite is true: newer posts push older ones out of sight, so important notices get lost."},{"t":"A mailing list for fixtures and announcements, because it pushes them to every inbox, and a discussion forum for questions, because its threads form a searchable archive; keep the list one-way to avoid reply-all overload, and appoint a forum moderator.","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. Each need gets the tool whose feature fits it, and the known weakness of each tool is managed."},{"t":"A mailing list for everything, because members prefer email.","fb":"Email suits announcements, but answers to questions get lost in inboxes and are not easily searched by future members."},{"t":"A discussion forum for everything, because forums are real-time.","fb":"Forums are asynchronous, and members would have to remember to visit the site to see fixtures."}]}
