     "model": "<p><b>(a)(i)</b> The school should send closure notices by <b>SMS</b>. SMS travels over the cellular network and works on any mobile phone, including basic phones, without a data plan or app, so every parent receives the notice within minutes, even if their Internet is down. Bulk SMS costs a small amount per message, but this is justified for urgent safety information.</p><p><b>(ii)</b> A <b>web-conferencing tool</b> such as Microsoft Teams is appropriate because it provides real-time video, audio and screen sharing, so teachers in Antriol and Barbados can discuss lessons face to face and share slides without the cost of flights. A drawback is that it needs a stable connection; if video freezes, staff can switch it off and continue with audio, and the meeting can be recorded.</p><p><b>(iii)</b> A <b>discussion forum</b> is best because questions and answers are organised into threads by topic and stored permanently, so next year's students can search and read earlier explanations. It needs a teacher to moderate posts for accuracy and respectful language.</p><p><b>(b)</b> SMS is asynchronous; web conferencing is real-time; the discussion forum is asynchronous.</p>",
