   "teacherTip": "<p>Common errors: defining knowledge as \"a lot of information\" (it is the <b>use</b> of information for decision making); listing characteristics such as \"timeliness, accuracy\" without explaining the effect on the decision; naming the IPOS stages without describing them in the scenario (CXC caps a stated-only list); forgetting <b>feedback</b>. For \"justify\", every tool needs a reason linked to the scenario (power cuts, no mobile data).</p>"
